
# Transaction Managers
- Transaction Manager is core component in transaction, it is responsible for managing the transactions.
  it is responsible for getting transaction, commiting a transaction and rolling back a transaction
- All the transaction operations transaction manager handle inside spring boot.
- Transaction Managers are the interface.

- public interface TransactionManager{            //This is just a parent interface.

}

- public interface PlatformTransactionManager extends TransactionManager{
    public void getTransaction();
    public void commit();
    public void rollback();
}

- now Abstract class AbstractPlatformTransactionManager provides the implementation of 
  getTransaction(), commit(), and rollback() methods.

- now this abstract class is used by different transaction managers(which are concrete classes) such as

- DataSource TransactionManager
- Hibernate TransactionManager
- JPA TransactionManager
- JTA TransactionManager
- JDBC TransactionManager

- So spring will choose one between them, most commen it chooes JPA TransactionManager at runtime.


# Types of TransactionManagers

1) Declarative TransactionManager
2) Programmatic TransactionManager

1) Declarative TransactionManager: 
 - Declarative means declear a annoation and job is done.
 - Transaction Management happens through Annotations
 - @Transactional
 - Spring boot will choose appropriate transaction manager.
 - We can create explicit transaction manager and tell spring to choose that.
Example:
 @Transactionl(transactionManager = "transactionManager")

 2) Programmatic TransactionManager
 - Handle Transaction progamtically/manually through code
 - Flexible but difficult to maintain
 - There are two approches for Programmatic TransactionManager

